{% extends 'layouts/page.njk' %}

{% block pageContent %}
  {{ appHeading({
    text: heading
  }) }}

  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <p class="govuk-body">
        This privacy notice explains how the Marine Management Organisation
        (MMO) and other UK fisheries authorities collect and use your
        personal data when you use the Under 10 Metre Catch Recording
        Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="who-collects-your-data">Who collects your data</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        The Marine Management Organisation (MMO) is the lead service owner
        and data controller for this service.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        MMO works with fisheries authorities across the UK and Crown
        Dependencies to manage and regulate fisheries. These organisations
        may process personal data collected through this service where
        required to carry out their statutory responsibilities.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="what-personal-data-we-collect">What personal data we collect</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">To provide this service, we collect and process:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>your name</li>
        <li>your address</li>
        <li>your email address</li>
        <li>information about vessels you own or operate</li>
        <li>catch record information you submit through the service</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        You must ensure that the information you provide is accurate and
        kept up to date.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="why-we-collect-your-data">Why we collect your data</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">We collect and use your personal data to:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>provide the Under 10 Metre Catch Recording Service</li>
        <li>record and manage catch information</li>
        <li>meet legal requirements relating to fisheries management and regulation</li>
        <li>verify information submitted through the service</li>
        <li>prevent and detect fraud</li>
        <li>support monitoring, enforcement and compliance activities</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="our-legal-basis-for-processing">Our legal basis for processing</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        We process personal data because we are required to do so to carry
        out tasks in the public interest and to comply with legal
        obligations relating to fisheries management and regulation.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        This includes legislation governing catch recording, fisheries
        monitoring and the management of marine resources.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="who-we-share-your-data-with">Who we share your data with</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">We may share your data with:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>fisheries authorities across the United Kingdom</li>
        <li>Crown Dependency fisheries authorities</li>
        <li>Defra and its agencies</li>
        <li>public bodies responsible for auditing, regulation or enforcement</li>
        <li>organisations where sharing is required by law</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        We will only share personal information where there is a lawful
        basis to do so.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        We will not allow any unwarranted breach of confidentiality and will
        process your information in accordance with UK data protection
        legislation.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="how-we-protect-your-data">How we protect your data</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Your personal information is processed securely using appropriate
        technical and organisational measures designed to protect it from
        unauthorised access, loss or misuse.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="how-long-we-keep-your-data">How long we keep your data</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        We keep your information in accordance with our records management
        and retention policies.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Information may be retained for longer where there is a legal
        requirement or where it is needed for:
      </p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>audits</li>
        <li>investigations or complaints</li>
        <li>legal proceedings</li>
        <li>scientific or historical research</li>
        <li>matters that establish an important precedent</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="what-happens-if-you-do-not-provide-your-data">What happens if you do not provide your data</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Providing the information requested by this service is necessary to
        meet legal obligations relating to catch recording and fisheries
        management.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        If you do not provide the required information, you may not be able
        to use the service or comply with these legal requirements.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="automated-decision-making">Automated decision-making</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Your information is not used to make decisions solely by automated
        means without human involvement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="international-transfers">International transfers</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Your personal data is not normally transferred outside the United
        Kingdom or European Economic Area (EEA).
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        In limited circumstances, data may be transferred where there is a
        lawful basis and appropriate safeguards are in place.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Under UK data protection legislation, you have rights relating to
        your personal information, including the right to:
      </p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>request access to your personal data</li>
        <li>request correction of inaccurate data</li>
        <li>request erasure of personal data in certain circumstances</li>
        <li>restrict how your data is processed in certain circumstances</li>
        <li>object to processing in certain circumstances</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        You can find out more about your rights on the Information
        Commissioner's Office (ICO) website.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="contact-us">Contact us</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">If you have any questions about how your personal data is used, contact:</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"><strong>Data Protection Manager</strong></p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Marine Management Organisation</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Lancaster House</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Hampshire Court</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Monarch Road</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Newcastle upon Tyne</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">NE4 7YH</p>
      <p class="govuk-body">Email: dataprotection@marinemanagement.org.uk</p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="data-protection-officer">Data Protection Officer</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">The MMO's Data Protection Officer can be contacted at:</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"><strong>Data Protection Officer</strong></p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Seacole Building</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">2 Marsham Street</p>
      <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">London</p>
      <p class="govuk-body">SW1P 4DF</p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="complaints">Complaints</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        If you are unhappy with how your personal data has been handled, you
        can make a complaint to the
        <a class="govuk-link" href="https://ico.org.uk">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}

